          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Recall that propositions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mutually+exclusive+propositions"} mutually exclusive
            if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ¬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg (P \wedge Q)
            holds. Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+propositions"} type of propositions
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                    %mo ,
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathrm{Prop}, \mathrm{El})
            %strong
              type of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mutually+exclusive+propositions"} mutually exclusive propositions
            is given by the type
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                    %mo ±
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi P
                        %mo +
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi P
                        %mo −
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ¬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mo +
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Prop}_\pm \coloneqq \sum_{P^+:\mathrm{Prop}} \sum_{P^-:\mathrm{Prop}} \mathrm{El}(\neg (P^+ \wedge P^-))
          %p
            We denote the two projection functions as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                    %mo ±
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^+:\mathrm{Prop}_\pm \to \mathrm{Prop}
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo −
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                      %mo ±
                    %mo →
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^-:\mathrm{Prop}_\pm \to \mathrm{Prop}
          %p
            In the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antithesis+interpretation"} antithesis interpretation
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+logic"} affine logic
            into
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is interpreted as a pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mo +
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (P^+, P^-)
            of mutually exclusive propositions. Similarly, an affine predicate
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            on a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is interpreted as a pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mo +
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (P^+, P^-)
            of predicates on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            in intuitionistic logic which are pointwise mutually exclusive in that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ¬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg (P^+(x) \wedge P^-(x))
            holds for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                      %mo ±
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P:A \to \mathrm{Prop}_\pm
          %h2#affine_logic_of_mutually_exclusive_propositions Affine logic of mutually exclusive propositions
          %p
            We have the following propositional and predicate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+logic"} affine
            logical operations on mutually exclusive propositions:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth"} truth
              is an element of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                      %mo ±
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Prop}_\pm
              defined as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ⊤
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊥
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \coloneqq (\top, \bot)
          %p
            We say that a pair of mutually exclusive propositions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mo +
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (P^+, P^-)
            holds if there is an element
