                  %mi P
                  %mo ⊞
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} !P \coloneqq P \boxtimes P \quad ?P \coloneqq P \boxplus P
          %p
            The type of mutually exclusive propositions is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/De+Morgan+algebra"} De Morgan algebra
            where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+lattice"} distributive lattice
            structure is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+conjunction"} additive conjunction
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+disjunction"} additive disjunction
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+logic"} affine logic
            of mutually exclusive propositions, and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
            is given by the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+negation"} linear negation
          %h3#excluded_middle Excluded middle
          %p
            Suppose that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/law+of+excluded+middle"} law of excluded middle
            holds in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intuitionistic+logic"} intuitionistic logic
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+logic"} classical logic
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Prop}
